Archons can indeed.  Archons, however, are not a "guaranteed" monster on
any of the Planes; on Astral, all the As that are generated are
specifically called out as "Angel".  If you move briskly through the
Planes (and you really, really should when possible, just as a general
'good play' concept), there just won't be time for very many random
monsters to spawn -- and the chances of any single random monster being
an Archon are very, very low.

In my games on NAO, I think I saw exactly three Archons on all my ascension
runs, and only two were on the Planes; both on the Plane of Fire.  I teleported 
past the first to the stairs with ctrl-T, and when the other two came close, I
teleported them away with a quick wand zap.

So much for Archons.  Nasty monster?  Yup.  Binary solution?  Yup.

I'm working on how to make them more meaningful in Spork.  Making them
resist teleportation is the obvious solution, but I dislike that plan
since it's the classic RPG road of "ha, ha, the bosses are immune to all
the cool status spells you get during the game."  

Making more things worth teleporting away (such that the player may be out 
of charges by the time the Archon shows up) seems to be a much better plan
that _doesn't_ penalize the player for being creative.

(I do the same thing to the vanilla Medusa Titan, when possible; usually
something has dropped a single teleport wand by then, and so I have a
few charges.  The Titan is worth one of those charges; once he's trapped
on an island in the middle of nowhere, he won't be summoning jack.)

